 already won the 200 back in LA, and had pouted on the victory podium, upset with his winning time. It earned him boos from the crowd and the media did not portray him kindly, calling him a sore winner. This time he smiled and acted more appreciative of the gold. Behind him " [:a {:href "/athletes/51617"} "Dave Wilson"] " of the US won silver and " [:a {:href "/athletes/46045"} "Mike West"] " of Canada took bronze."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The fourth spot went to New Zealand’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/49630"} "Gary Hurring"] " who was hoping to become New Zealand’s first Olympic swimming medalist since his mother, " [:a {:href "/athletes/49611"} "Jean Stewart"] ", won a bronze in the 100 back for women in 1952. From a line of backstroke swimmers, Hurring’s father, " [:a {:href "\\athletes\\show\\49631"} "Lincoln"] ", also swam the 100 back at the 1952 (and 1956) Olympics. A few weeks after the Olympics, Dirk Richter won the Friendship Games 100 back in 55.67."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "454"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51287"} "Rick Carey"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "55.74 (1 h7)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "55.79 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "490"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51617"} "Dave Wilson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "56.71 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "56.35 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silve